{"skill":{"slug":"android-adb","displayName":"ADB Connection"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770159228342,"changelog":"Initial release of android-automation skill.\n\n- Control Android devices via ADB, with support for UI layout analysis using uiautomator and visual feedback via screencap.\n- Includes guidance for connecting devices via USB and wireless debugging on Android 11+.\n- Provides example commands for launching apps, interacting with UI elements (tap, text input, key events, swipe), and visual verification through screenshots.\n- Offers tips for advanced workflows including UI hierarchy analysis and reliable input methods.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2105,"sha256":"b56269b935bf89694b62a6c124372882daf7cd02a77fc9d9dc2ef5b270681a58","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1869,"sha256":"f84b328f943afef87f83acb29365c180e121b45acaa0fe57b9b7e77702551357","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789031855318,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f4fa2f552169e0eae74d44121d8839e312acdf23338d0ee6f558a9a6d71e9de2","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f4fa2f552169e0eae74d44121d8839e312acdf23338d0ee6f558a9a6d71e9de2","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: android-adb\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It provides instructions for controlling Android devices using standard ADB commands, including UI analysis and screenshots. All described actions, such as `adb shell` commands and `adb pull` for device-generated files, are directly aligned with the stated purpose of Android automation. There is no evidence of prompt injection against the agent, data exfiltration from the agent's host, malicious execution, or any other intent to compromise the agent's environment or unrelated systems.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161194213},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789031855318},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Android ADB automation guide, with powerful but clearly disclosed device-control capabilities.","dimensions":[{"detail":"ADB access can control a connected Android device, enter text, inspect UI layout, and capture screenshots, but those effects are expected and disclosed for this skill type.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a single Markdown skill file with no bundled scripts, dependencies, installer, or executable payload.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions are limited to connection setup and common ADB workflows, with no prompt overrides, hidden role changes, or unrelated agent behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill does not request persistence, modify agent tools, install services, store credentials, or write cross-session memory.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Android automation through ADB, uiautomator, and screencap; the listed capabilities directly match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Only use this skill when you intend to let the agent operate Android devices you connect through ADB. Review commands before execution, especially taps, text entry, screenshots, and wireless ADB connections, because they can affect apps and accounts on the device.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031855318}}}}}